{
  "schema": "zetesis.refinement.evaluation.check.v1",
  "checkedOn": "2026-10-03",
  "scope": "The extracted scalar reference checker is refined under fixed-observation and scalar/sequence models. Generated owner checks and cloning obey explicit immutable-heap contracts. Actual zero initialization establishes the empty packed subset. These operations compose with original evaluation, root checking, atom selection and completed proper-subset search to decide answer-set membership under explicit admission and storage premises. Actual failed roots and returned countermodels exclude membership. Typed interruptions do not establish a Boolean verdict. A separate checked event model permits changing observations and fallible reservation; it is not installed in the extracted checker. The generated admission step called by Theory::new computes the authored validator, including the dimension and padded-count checks, and returns the supplied data unchanged; its node and root validators compute the authored scans for every represented slice, and a node refusal reports the error of the first refused node. Data returned by the admission step supplies the ordered-children and bounded-root premises, which remain premises of the composed theorems. The generated Theory::new wrapper is parameterized by a supplied allocation operation through an audited scoped binder, with its stock body unchanged. A completed constructor return establishes actual admission and allocation; typed refusal is exactly admission refusal, and backend failure or divergence is preserved. An explicit returned-value contract supplies the stored data and structural premises; a separate per-invocation fresh heap transition supports ownership. The generated frozen-reduct constructor and public query take supplied fallible reservation operations through four further audited scoped binders, with their stock bodies unchanged. Actual completed construction establishes candidate retention and the original-truth mask; actual completed public querying checks ownership, polls, reserves and decides Ferraris reduct satisfaction. Their composition needs represented interpretations, ordered nodes and bounded roots, but neither candidate modelhood, a tested-subset premise nor assumed mask agreement. Construction and query have separate supplied providers, limits and fixed observation tokens, and each starts zero counters. A completed freeze charges exactly one work unit per node; private query evaluation and root scanning share the actual returned work. Typed reservation refusal, backend failure and divergence remain distinct from completed verdicts. No default provider, allocation-success assumption or changing allocator history is installed. The actual generic Interpretation::new and its fixed-length scalar-bound insertion helper are now exported directly. The constructor phase equation preserves word counting, fallible reservation, resize, iterable conversion, actual insertion and final shared-theory clone. A completed constructor derives those successful inner calls, exact word count, actual returned slice and retained theory, without assuming iterator correctness or allocation success. The actual generic insertion loop now terminates under sufficient word storage and a finite-input contract consisting only of actual iterator next observations. Its returned words are exactly the insertion of the bounded prefix, with unchanged word count and Atom refusal at the first invalid coordinate. The invalid-head law requires no contract on later iterator calls; the first None ends insertion without requiring fusion. Actual checked scalar operations, slice reads and updates establish each insertion rather than assuming a word-update result. Successful actual construction, under the explicit contract that successful reservation preserves its empty input sequence, derives retained theory, bounded input atoms and exact packed words; the shared packing and extracted membership laws supply exact storage, zero padding and query answers. The imported owned-vector conversion and iterator discharge the finite-input contract without an input-validity, ordering or distinctness premise. No allocation success, unrestricted-iterator termination or returned terminal iterator state is assumed or claimed. The actual public oracle::check is now extracted directly and its completed return supplies the actual ownership, polling, reservation, evaluation, root-scan, selection, initialization and search calls. Under immutable-heap consistency, admitted theory structure, exact candidate storage and explicit successful-empty-sequence contracts for selection and word reservations, the returned Stable verdict is equivalent to Ferraris answer-set membership. Negative verdicts retain the actual failing asserted root or proper-subset reduct witness; returned statistics come from the actual final Work. The search frame preserves owner, storage length, controls and limits while counters do not decrease, including internal typed stops. Wrong ownership precedes polling; a stopped initial poll precedes reservation; a first typed reservation refusal maps to Allocation. One pure reservation provider and fixed observation tokens interpret the entire generated wrapper. The completed theorem does not itself establish projection of arbitrary runtime allocation/control histories, or total completion for arbitrary external providers. The subject-bound check_interpretation API wrapper, changing runtime observations, grounding, solver enumeration and GPU execution remain outside this proof.",
